COMPRESSION SERVICES AGREEMENT

This Compression Services Agreement is entered into as of ___________, 1999, (together with all schedules, appendices and exhibits, if any, hereto attached and made a part hereof, this "Agreement"), between ____________________, a ____________ corporation ("Contractor"), and TRANSWESTERN PIPELINE COMPANY, a Delaware corporation ("Customer"), each a "Party" and together the "Parties."

Whereas, Customer desires to purchase compression services on demand; and

Whereas, Contractor desires to provide on demand compression service; 

Whereas, the Parties acknowledge that the compression services to be provided by Contractor to Customer hereunder are functionally related to the natural gas pipeline system of Customer and to the transportation services provided by Customer as an interstate gas pipeline company under Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") jurisdiction.  The parties further acknowledge that the FERC will continue to exercise regulatory authority over the services provided by Customer, and, through its regulation of Customer, the assets owned by Contractor.  In that regard, it is the Parties' intent that the requirements, set forth herein, that Contractor must receive written approval from Customer prior to undertaking certain actions with respect to ownership of the assets which shall not restrict the scope of Contractor's actions as owner of the assets, but solely facilitate and ensure continued regulatory compliance; and

Whereas, Contractor and Customer are parties to that certain Purchase and Sale Agreement dated ___________(the “Purchase Agreement”) involving the sale of certain assets.  For purposes of this Agreement, "Assets" shall mean, collectively, (a) the assets described on Appendix 1of this Agreement and (b) any assets modified, repaired, replaced or exchanged as contemplated in Sections 8 and 12 of this Agreement and as described on any schedules prepared pursuant to Section 30(e) of this Agreement.


Now Therefore, the Parties hereto acknowledge and agree as follows:


ON DEMAND COMPRESSION.  Subject to and on the terms and conditions herein set forth, Contractor hereby agrees to provide on demand compression services, including, without limitation, the necessary equipment and operating services described in Appendix 2, as the same may be amended from time to time (collectively, the "Services"). 

 

TERM AND TERMINATION.  

2.1  Term.  The period for which the Services shall be provided pursuant to this Agreement (as may be extended or sooner terminated pursuant to the provisions hereof, the "Term") shall commence upon Closing as defined in thePurchase Agreement(“the Effective Date”), between the Parties and continue without interruption through the earlier of (a) ___________, 20___at 11:59 p.m. or l (b) 12:00 a.m. on the date on which Customer repurchases the  Assets in accordance with Section 6 of this Agreement, unless otherwise terminated pursuant to Section 2.2 (a) or 2.2 (b) below (the "Term").  This Agreement may be extended by the mutual agreement of the parties.  Upon expiration of the Term of this Agreement, any monies or other charges due and owing either Party shall be paid and any corrections or adjustments to payments previously made shall be determined and paid within sixty (60) days.  Notwithstanding the foregoing, all indemnity and confidentiality rights and obligations hereunder shall survive the Term.  The Parties' obligations provided in this Agreement shall remain in effect for the purpose of complying herewith.

